    "summary": "Feather god&#039;s eye. Disk made of strips of cane (?), slightly concave. The concave side is covered with small bunches of feathers: yellow O&#039;o feathers in a border around the outside edge, red iwi feathers within this, surrounding a central disk of pearl shell (representing the white of an eye), and a patch of black feathers above the pearl shell (representing an eyebrow). The pearl shell disk is pierced and held in place by a wooden peg, with a rounded tip (representing the pupil of an eye). On the back is fixed a plaited band of vegetable fibre, ending in a thin plaited fibre loop.",
